From e249c3fe7a82667aea4ae56a3f49b461ad89c3b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Randy Northrup <randy.northrup@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:55:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] usb: xhci-tegra: re-probe through the driver core in
 hcd_reinit

xhci_reinit_work() calls tegra_xusb_remove() and tegra_xusb_probe()
directly. The driver core never sees the unbind, so the devm resources
from the first probe stay allocated, and the re-probe fails:

  tegra-xusb 70090000.xusb: can't request region for resource
  [mem 0x70099000-0x70099fff]

That leaves USB dead until reboot, which is the opposite of what
en_hcd_reinit is for. Use device_release_driver() + device_attach()
instead. remove() frees xhci, which contains this work item, but doesn't
cancel it, so nothing waits on the running work and only pdev is used
after the unbind.

Tested on a Switch Lite (4.9.140-l4t): the old path reproducibly fails as
above. The same driver-core unbind/bind, done from an out-of-tree module
after "HC died", brings the controller back, and a replugged DisplayLink
dock enumerates and works again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-tegra.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-tegra.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-tegra.c
index 970a984e..bea670ff 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-tegra.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-tegra.c
@@ -5426,9 +5426,19 @@ static void xhci_reinit_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	xhci->xhc_state |= XHCI_STATE_DYING;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&xhci->lock, flags);
 
-	tegra_xusb_remove(pdev);
+	/*
+	 * Go through the driver core. Calling tegra_xusb_remove() and
+	 * tegra_xusb_probe() directly never releases the devm resources of
+	 * the first probe, so the re-probe fails with "can't request region"
+	 * and USB stays dead until reboot. remove() frees xhci (and this
+	 * work item) but doesn't cancel it, so only pdev is used from here.
+	 */
+	get_device(&pdev->dev);
+	device_release_driver(&pdev->dev);
 	usleep_range(10, 20);
-	tegra_xusb_probe(pdev);
+	if (device_attach(&pdev->dev) != 1)
+		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "re-probe after hcd_reinit failed\n");
+	put_device(&pdev->dev);
 
 	/* probe will set recovery_in_progress to false */
 }
